      "category": "electrical",
      "title": "Infotainment System Freezing and Audio Dropouts",
      "description": "The XT4 infotainment system (CUE) experiences screen freezing, intermittent audio muting, and climate control display glitches. The sound can go completely mute at random times, even affecting OnStar calls. The climate control display occasionally shows \"Climate Off\" incorrectly after startup. Cadillac released a fix in July 2021 for black screen/freezing issues.",
      "solution": "Verify the concern by checking for HMI/Radio module faults with GDS2 and confirming the current software levels for the infotainment system, radio amplifier, and related communication modules. For 2019-2023 XT4 models with freezing, black screen, muted audio, or incorrect climate display behavior, Cadillac’s repair is typically to reprogram the radio/HMI modules with the latest GM calibration released in mid-2021 and perform a battery support-maintained software update, followed by a hard reset and function test of audio, OnStar, and HVAC display pages. If symptoms remain after programming, inspect the infotainment fuse/power-ground circuits and replace the radio display/HMI module only if diagnostics show the hardware is failing; software updates usually run about $150-$300 out of warranty, while module replacement can raise the repair to roughly $800-$1,500 depending on part and programming needs.",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "symptoms": [
        "Audio suddenly goes mute during driving",
        "Touchscreen freezes or goes black",
        "Climate control display shows \"Climate Off\" erroneously",
        "Vehicle status page freezes when pressed",
        "OnStar audio not working during active call"
      ],
